body:
A Data Fiduciary may process personal data without consent for:
(a) the specified purpose for which the Data Principal **voluntarily provided** her data and has not objected;
(b) the State/instrumentalities providing a **subsidy, benefit, service, certificate, licence or permit**, where she previously consented for such purposes, or the data is already held in a government database/register notified by the Central Government, subject to government-issued processing standards;
(c) performance by the State of any function under law, or in the interest of **sovereignty/integrity of India** or **security of the State**;
(d) fulfilling a legal disclosure obligation to the State;
(e) compliance with a **judgment/decree/court order** (India or, for civil/contractual claims, abroad);
(f) responding to a **medical emergency** threatening life/health;
(g) providing medical treatment/health services during an **epidemic/outbreak/public health threat**;
(h) ensuring safety/assistance during a **disaster** or breakdown of public order (as defined under the Disaster Management Act, 2005);
(i) **employment purposes**, or safeguarding the employer from loss/liability (e.g., corporate espionage, trade-secret protection), or providing a service/benefit sought by an employee.
